node #pragma doc It limits the first derivative of the signal passing through. The output changes no faster than the specified limit. 
     Let us call Rate the derivative ((RL_Input-pre(RL_Output))/DeltaT. 
     If Rate > Rising, then RL_Output equals (Rising* DeltaT + pre(RL_Output)) 
     If Rate < Falling, then RL_Output equals (Falling* DeltaT + pre(RL_Output)) 
     Otherwise, RL_Output=RL_Input #end RateLimiter (Input: 'T;
                                                     Rising: 'T;
                                                     Falling: 'T;
                                                     deltaT: 'T;)
  returns (Output: 'T last = Input;)
  where 'T float
{
  diagram
    (#1 expr last 'Output
